{"duration_api_ms":131286,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2c47bdd9-9643-4085-8f7c-96678e5a4ba5","total_cost_usd":0.18059799999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13776,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12549,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13776,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12549,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13776},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12549,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13776,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18059799999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7117,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by flight-path angle and binds at a limit of 12 g. At D=3.3, b=1.17 and cone 70, g is 11.85 at -3.5 deg and 12.01 at -3.6 deg. Changing bluntness, cone angle or D by small amounts moves g by less than 0.05. Every point on the feasible front sits at the corner of the bounds: cone 70 (max), bluntness about 1.17, D about 3.3-3.37. That corner is capped by the heatshield mass fraction, whose margin falls about 0.58 per metre of D and does not depend on gamma. Larger D and slightly higher b lower both heat flux and bondline temperature. Bluntness 1.22 and 1.25 at cone 70 fail on aero surrogate extrapolation, while 1.20 works. The remaining headroom is D up to about 3.38 with b=1.2, cone 70, swept along the gamma trade-off from about -1.5 to -3.55 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-d3a7fa99fcee (D3.3) vs C-d706f33c18bc (D3.35), both b1.17 at -3.5 deg: heat flux 284.5k -> 278.4k, bondline 393.5 -> 392.6 K. Larger D helps both objectives.\",\"C-70f28f0eabf2 (D3.1), C-cde6c1e46d6d (D3.2), C-c050b796618a (D3.3) at -3.6 deg: heat 314k / 300k / 287k, bondline 396.2 / 394.3 / 392.5 K. Larger D is better on both axes.\",\"Mass margin vs D at b1.17: 0.0489 at 3.3, 0.0199 at 3.35, 0.0081 at 3.37 (C-a8aec30c684b). The extrapolated zero is about D=3.384. b1.2 gives a slightly higher margin (0.0497 at 3.3, C-cbb67c388863).\",\"C-cbb67c388863 (b1.2, -3.55) beats the interpolated b1.17 series at the same gamma: 284.4k / 392.8 K vs about 285.8k / 393.0 K.\",\"Same-D gamma sweep at D3.3/b1.17: C-5644bff69a09 (-1.6) 239k / 418 K to C-d3a7fa99fcee (-3.5) 284.5k / 393.5 K. g reaches 12.0 at about -3.59 deg (C-c050b796618a, margin -0.001).\",\"C-425c523a5086, C-5b57439845df and C-e605b64e0636 (b1.22-1.25, cone 70) are rejected for extrapolation. The b limit at cone 70 lies between 1.20 and 1.22.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies on the data plus prior Sutton-Graves reasoning. Peak heating falls as nose radius (b*D) grows, and the heat load falls as ballistic coefficient drops, so a larger D at high b and cone 70 helps both objectives. Steeper entry shortens the heating pulse and lowers bondline temperature, but raises peak heat flux and g, and g caps gamma near -3.57 deg. The geometry is therefore pushed to the mass-fraction edge (D about 3.38) and gamma is swept along the g limit. That shifts the whole front toward lower heat flux and lower temperature. A few probes test cone angle, b just above 1.2, and the mass edge.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass-fraction edge near D=3.384 is extrapolated linearly from three points. The D3.38 points near -3.55 deg have about 0.03 g of margin, and g may rise slightly with D. The cone-angle probes are not backed by data at high b, and mass or aero behaviour may differ. The b>1.2 probes may hit the surrogate hull and fail. Predicted heat-flux and temperature gains from D use an exponent fitted only on D 3.1-3.35.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Steep end of the front: D at the mass edge, b1.2, cone 70, gamma just inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether larger D at b1.2 gives a front-dominating point while g stays below 12.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly less steep, so more g margin than the -3.55 deg point, at D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Confirms the D3.38 improvement over C-d706f33c18bc (278.4k / 392.6 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma at D3.38 to fill the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between the steep and mid-gamma points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-steep point at D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the low-g region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -3.0 at D3.38. Compare with C-c15b7aa0a4cb (272k / 398.8 K).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Quantifies the D and b gain in the middle of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -2.75 at D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the mid range.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -2.5 at D3.38. Compare with C-8c42ec2e069f (259.7k / 405 K).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the mid range.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -2.25 at D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the shallow-mid range.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -2.0 at D3.38. Compare with C-57afc5c7f317 (247.8k / 412 K).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the shallow range.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -1.8 at D3.38, filling the low-heat-flux end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":234500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the shallow range.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow extreme of the gamma bound (-1.5) at D3.38, extending the low-heat-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":418.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front to the minimum-heat-flux end. Bondline temperature rises toward the 450 K limit as gamma gets shallower.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"D3.384 at the extrapolated mass-fraction edge, to locate the boundary.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the linear extrapolation of the mass margin, which is near zero here. Feasibility is the key unknown.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly smaller D (3.36) at the steep end, a safer alternative to the D3.38 steep points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a robust feasible point at the steep end with good mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Probes bluntness just above 1.2 (1.21) for a small further heating gain, staying near the known hull edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the surrogate hull boundary between b1.20 (ok) and b1.22 (fails). It may return no metrics.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Tests a cone angle below 70 (67 deg) at D3.3 and b1.2 to see whether cone 70 really is optimal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone angle is an untested lever at high b. C-3e9a8e44ddcf (cone 69) hinted at slightly worse heating.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Larger cone-angle step down (64 deg) to establish the trend and the mass response.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether cone angle trades heat flux against mass margin differently from the D and b levers.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Probes higher bluntness (1.25) at a lower cone angle (62 deg), in case the hull boundary in (b, cone) is not a fixed b limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.0,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap test of whether higher nose radius is reachable away from the cone-70 corner. It probably fails on extrapolation.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"D3.38 at -3.53 deg, between the -3.5 and -3.55 points, as a hedge against g running over 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Resolves how much g margin remains at D3.38 near the steep limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-D (3.34) point at gamma -3.2, adding coverage with more mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D sensitivity between 3.3 and 3.38 at intermediate gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -1.65 at D3.38, filling between the -1.5 and -1.8 points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage at the low-heat-flux end. Compare with C-5644bff69a09 (239k / 418.4 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":86942,"type":"result","duration_ms":131317,"uuid":"fe44702d-a1f6-45bf-9e8a-490ae123755e","ttft_stream_ms":1490,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":1490,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
